The ADR-0017 section 3a walk is three-valued, and only `False` -- "ran to
completion AND accounted for the value at every step" -- may ever license
removing a reported flow. It was also being returned when the index held
nothing at all about a definition:

    _ddg_taint_reaches("f", [1], [9], {})  ->  False

reproduced live. The walk read `ddg_uses.get(...)` and, on an empty result,
continued WITHOUT setting `escaped`. Every other way of losing the value
flags itself; this one did not.

Two return values, three causes. A negative walk means (1) the value goes
nowhere near a sink, (2) it left the tracked chain into a container section
7b excludes, or (3) the construct that defined it was never modelled, so no
use was ever recorded. Only (1) is exhaustion. (2) leaves an escape to
classify; (3) leaves SILENCE, so no work on the escape vocabulary would ever
have surfaced it. cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents a matching gap -- `if err
:= do(); err != nil` initializers are invisible to def/use -- and 700 of
caddy's 6,596 `if` statements carry a call there.

Behaviour-neutral today, verified not assumed: the sole production call site
is `_ddg_taint_reaches(...) is True`, so `False` and `None` already collapse.
The recall corpus, the only test that runs the real pipeline end to end, is
unchanged. The change can only prevent a future false negative.

The population is narrower than the item filed, and the correction is
measured. The barren branch is reachable only for SEED lines -- every other
frontier entry is membership-tested before being appended -- and
propagate_taint_ddg gates the walk on `source_tracked = any(...)`, so a
source whose only call line is untracked never reaches the walk at all. The
production-reachable shape is a source with >=2 call sites where at least one
is untracked. The caddy trace recorded on the item does NOT reach this path:
run through a reimplementation of the pre-fix walk beside the current one it
returns None on BOTH, because the intermediate line fails the membership test
one step earlier and hits the escape branch.

This is the conservative floor, not the structural fix. Refutation should be
coverage-gated -- forfeited for any function whose CFG statement extents fail
to cover every call node in its body -- which catches the class mechanically
rather than by enumerating known gaps. Not implemented here.

Retires test_barren_seed_line_is_skipped, which documented the defect as
intended behaviour and whose assertion passed for an unrelated reason (the
None came from a later escape, not the barren seed), so it never exercised
the branch it named. Replaced by the bare repro plus an isolation pair: a
closed cycle from a tracked seed yields False, and adding one barren seed
degrades it to None.

